# <%= app_name_camel_case %>

## Setup

- install Elixir, Erlang and Node using [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev)
  - install mise using either `curl https://mise.run | sh` or `brew install mise`
  - make sure to activate it
  - run `mise install`<%= if phoenix do %>
- install Tidewave MCP Proxy (https://elixirdrops.net/d/UAo4BtYi)<% end %><%= if ecto do %>
- start PostgreSQL server<% end %><%= if phoenix do %>
- set environment variables in `.env` (see: [.env.sample](.env.sample))<% end %>
- run `mix setup`
<%= if phoenix do %>- start Phoenix server with `mix phx.server`

Now you can visit [`localhost:4000`](http://localhost:4000) from your browser.<% end %>

## Docs

- execute `mix docs --formatter html --open`

It will open documentation in your browser.

## Running tests

- run `mix coveralls` or `mix coveralls.html`

## Contributing

Make sure to execute `make ci` in order to run all the checks before committing the code.
